{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issues_index.json'\nwith open(p) as f: data=json.load(f)\nitems=data if isinstance(data,list) else data.get('issues', [])\nfor n in (4203,1905,4029,3036,3138):\n    item=next((x for x in items if x.get('number')==n),None)\n    if item:\n        print(json.dumps({k:item.get(k) for k in ('number','title','body','state','state_reason','author_association')}, ensure_ascii=False))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"number\": 4203, \"title\": \"Question: When will Pull Requests be enabled for external contributors?\", \"body\": \"Hi! \\n\\nI noticed a broken link in and fixed in the root documentation.\\n\\nI have fixed this on my fork and would love to submit a Pull Request for it, as this will be my very first open-source PR! However, I noticed that Pull Requests are currently restricted to repository collaborators. \\n\\nCould you please let me know when PRs will be enabled for external contributors so I can submit it? \\n\\nThank you!\\n\", \"state\": null, \"state_reason\": \"completed\", \"author_association\": null}\n{\"number\": 1905, \"title\": \"[BUG] In Jupyter mode have the link target to \\\"_blank\\\"\", \"body\": \"You may find a solution to your problem in the [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) or [issues](https://github.com/willmcgugan/rich/issues).\\r\\n\\r\\n**Describe the bug**\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen using `jupyter.print([link=http://my.cool.link.com]cool link[/link])` and when trying to follow the link it tries to open the link in the resulting cell and getting a broken link. I would suggest to fix this link rendering a bit:\\r\\nhttps://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/rich/jupyter.py#L66\\r\\nby adding the following (`target=\\\"_blank\\\"`):\\r\\n`text = f'<a href=\\\"{style.link}\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">{text}</a>'` so it will open the link in a new window\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Platform**\\r\\n<details>\\r\\n<summary>Click to expand</summary>\\r\\n\\r\\nWhat platform (Win/Linux/Mac) are you running on? What terminal software are you using?\\r\\n\\r\\nI may ask you to cut and paste the output of the following commands. It may save some time if you do it now.\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\npython -m rich.diagnose\\r\\npython -m rich._windows\\r\\npip freeze | grep rich\\r\\n```\\r\\n  \\r\\n</details>\\r\\n\", \"state\": null, \"state_reason\": \"completed\", \"author_association\": null}\n{\"number\": 4029, \"title\": \"Request: Enable PRs from forks for contributors\", \"body\": \"Hi Rich maintainers,\\\\n\\\\nI have a fix ready for mixed-width text handling in , but I currently can’t open a PR to the upstream repository from my fork.\\\\n\\\\nPR with the fix:\\\\nhttps://github.com/Siew-s-Capital/rich/pull/1\\\\n\\\\nCould you please either:\\\\n1) grant me collaborator access, **or**\\\\n2) enable PRs from forks for contributors\\\\n\\\\nso I can submit this change properly?\\\\n\\\\nThanks for your time and for maintaining Rich.\", \"state\": null, \"state_reason\": \"completed\", \"author_association\": null}\n{\"number\": 3036, \"title\": \"[BUG] Long link address is incorrect when it breaks into two lines in PyCharm\", \"body\": \"- [x] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions.\\r\\n- [x] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md).\\r\\n\\r\\n**Describe the bug**\\r\\n\\r\\nThere are two visible issues:\\r\\n1. If the displayed text is not \\\"url-like\\\", in PyCharm it will not be clickable. In Jupyter Lab it works fine.\\r\\n2. When the displayed text is too long and breaks into two lines:\\r\\n  2.1. In PyCharm, the actual link address will contain only the first line which is incorrect. \\r\\n  2.2. In Jupyter Lab the actual link address is complete and correct, but when I hover over the link with mouse, only the current line will show an underscore, while I expected to see both lines of the link underscored. (This is a minor cosmetic issue.)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Code**\\r\\n`from rich import print`\\r\\n`url = \\\"https://www.google.com/search?q=test\\\"`\\r\\n`text_url = \\\"https://www.google.com/search?q=test123\\\"`\\r\\n`text_long = \\\"https://www.google.com/search?q=test1aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaddddddddeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeefffffffffffffffffff\\\"`\\r\\n`text = \\\"aaaaaccccccc\\\"`\\r\\n`print(f\\\"My short link: [link={url}]{text_url}[/link]\\\")`\\r\\n`print(f\\\"My long link: [link={url}]{text_long}[/link]\\\")`\\r\\n`print(f\\\"My long link: [link={url}]{text}[/link]\\\")`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Output of the code**\\r\\n\\r\\nPyCharm output (for issue 1 and 2.1): link address contains only first line's content (`https://www.google.com/search?q=test1aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaddddddddeeeeeee`)\\r\\n<img width=\\\"484\\\" alt=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/Textualize/rich/assets/102001380/4c6f75d6-c75a-419e-a607-a1c3d58c530d\\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nJupyterLab output (for issue 2.2): only the first line has underscore when I hover over the first line\\r\\n<img width=\\\"359\\\" alt=\\\"image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/Textualize/rich/assets/102001380/232f8e57-04da-47b9-af3d-a66c71438809\\\">\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Platform**\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n<details>\\r\\n<summary>\", \"state\": null, \"state_reason\": \"completed\", \"author_association\": null}\n{\"number\": 3138, \"title\": \"[BUG] Link to local files with spaces in their path don't render in Console\", \"body\": \"- [x] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions.\\r\\n- [x] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md).\\r\\n\\r\\n**Describe the bug**\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen using `[link=<link>]<text>[/link]` to display a link in the console, it works well with local files **except** when these files have a space in it.\\r\\n\\r\\n1. By default, the console will not apply the `link` Style (the code does not enter in `Style.parse` for this)\\r\\n2. If we pass a URI (e.g. `file://my%20F/my%20Ffile.txt`), then rich replace `%20F` by `%25F20F` making the link unusable\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n```python\\r\\nfrom rich.console import Console\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\npath_without = r\\\"D:\\\\TOTO\\\\my_dir\\\\animals.txt\\\"\\r\\npath_with = r\\\"D:\\\\TOTO\\\\my_dir\\\\file with space.txt\\\"\\r\\nuri = \\\"file://\\\" + path_with.replace(\\\" \\\", \\\"%20F\\\").replace(\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\"/\\\")\\r\\nprint(f\\\"{uri=}\\\")\\r\\n\\r\\nconsole = Console()\\r\\nconsole.print(f\\\"Link #0: [link={path_without}]Local Path without space[/link]\\\")\\r\\nconsole.print(f\\\"Link #1: [link={path_with}]Local Path with space[/link]\\\")\\r\\nconsole.print(\\r\\n    f\\\"Link #2: [link={uri}]Local path with space as URI[/link] (including %20F)\\\"\\r\\n)\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n![image](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/assets/1401809/b02a8dae-4be9-40b3-9e11-08148296a8be)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Platform**\\r\\n\\r\\n<summary>Windows 11, Python 3.9, CMD  & Powershell</summary>\\r\\n\\r\\n<details>\\r\\nWhat platform (Win/Linux/Mac) are you running on? What terminal software are you using?\\r\\n```\\r\\n╭───────────────────────── <class 'rich.console.Console'> ─────────────────────────╮\\r\\n│ A high level console interface.                                                  │\\r\\n│                                                                                  │\\r\\n│ ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮ │\\r\\n│ │ <console width=116 ColorSystem.TRUECOLOR>                                    │ │\\r\\n│ ╰─────────────────────────────────────────────\", \"state\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"author_association\": null}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
